                <mxCell id="e-foot" value="A fork is a paired counterfactual on one history. Report that case, its substitutions, unverified writes, and limitations; unrelated ToB runs are not parallel comparison units.&amp;nbsp;&lt;div&gt;A fork with no substitutions must reproduce the source surface exactly; any difference means an unpinned dependency leaked into the pipeline.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Forks are causal and lazy: descendants are invalidated, independent events merge, eval blocks at target seq.&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontColor=#1971C2;fontSize=12;fontFamily=LXGW WenKai TC;" parent="1" vertex="1">
